# Environment variables

Configuration is read exclusively from environment variables. Defaults below are the application defaults. The deployed values are set per environment in the system's gitops-app repo (`system.yaml`: a component's `env`, and `replicas`, `resources` under `instances.<env>`).

## Core

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` | `{{ port }}` | HTTP port (`server.port`). |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Root log level (`logging.level.root`). |
| `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS` | `-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75` | JVM flags; keeps the heap inside the container memory limit. |
{%- if needs_database %}

## Database (PostgreSQL)

Set by the platform's `postgres` resource when the service declares `uses: [postgres]`; the defaults match `devbox run db-up`.

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `PGHOST` | `localhost` | Database host. |
| `PGPORT` | `5432` | Database port. |
| `PGDATABASE` | `{{ project_name | replace('-', '_') }}` | Database name. |
| `PGUSER` | `app` | Database user. |
| `PGPASSWORD` | `dev` | Database password (generated and injected from a Secret in the cluster, never committed). |
{%- endif %}
{%- if needs_observability %}

## Observability

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `OTEL_SDK_DISABLED` | `true` (image default) | Set to `false` to enable the OpenTelemetry Java agent. |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` | _(unset)_ | OTLP endpoint traces are exported to (required when the agent is enabled). |
| `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` | `{{ project_name }}` | Service name reported in traces. |
{%- endif %}

## Build / CI

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `NVD_API_KEY` | Optional NVD API key for `devbox run audit`. Set it (as a CI secret) to use OWASP Dependency-Check; unset, `audit` falls back to `trivy fs`. |
